   "text": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# release-notes\n\n## What it does\n\n`release-notes` drafts release notes from pull requests merged between two tags.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it to prepare a release draft from merged PRs. For prose edits, use `technical-writing`.\n\nThis skill runs only when you invoke it manually:\n\n```text\n/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>\n```\n\nFor example, with illustrative tags:\n\n```text\n/release-notes v1.0.0 v1.1.0\n```\n\n## How it works\n\nYou must be signed in to `gh`. The skill stops if `gh auth status` fails. Both tags must exist; if either is missing, it stops before drafting.\n\nThe skill gathers merged PRs, skips those labeled `skip-notes`, and groups the rest by Conventional Commit type. Features, fixes, and breaking changes come first.\n\nIf a PR has labels for multiple types, it goes in the group named by most of its labels. Ties follow label order.\n\nEvery breaking change needs a migration line. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n\n## What you get\n\nThe skill writes `RELEASE_NOTES.md` in your working tree and stops. It never publishes.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) Will it publish a release?\n(b) How do you run it?\n(c) What happens to a breaking change with no migration note?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (a) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
